The ``ctypes`` brain now gives the ``value`` argument of ``c_int``, ``c_char``,
``c_double`` and the other simple types the same default as at runtime
(``0``, ``0.0``, ``b"\x00"``, ``"\x00"`` or ``False``). ``apple = c_int()`` no
longer makes pylint emit ``no-value-for-parameter`` on interpreters where
``_ctypes`` is a built-in module, such as the uv and python-build-standalone
builds.

Refs #3482
